\fill[white] (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\fill[regionfill] (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,3.8);
\draw (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\node at (1.5,3.3) {$A$};
\node at (4.5,3.3) {$B$};
\node[anchor=north west] at (0.1,3.7) {$\xi$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

c. The union contains both whole circles. Its complement is outside both circles.

d. Intersecting the two complements keeps points outside $A$ and outside $B$.

Both parts give this shading:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{regionfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
