\fill[white] (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\fill[white] (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,3.8);
\draw (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\node at (1.5,3.3) {$A$};
\node at (4.5,3.3) {$B$};
\node[anchor=north west] at (0.1,3.7) {$\xi$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The regions are equal: $(A\cup B)'=A'\cap B'$.

examples.question_text:
The diagram shows members of a recreation club. $H$ is the hiking group and $C$ is the cycling group.
How many members are in:
a. $H$
b. $H\cap C$
c. $H'\cap C$
d. $H\cup C$
e. $(H\cup C)'$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,3.8);
\draw (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\node at (1.5,3.3) {$H$};
\node at (4.5,3.3) {$C$};
\node[anchor=north west] at (0.1,3.7) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.7,1.8) {$16$};
\node at (3,1.8) {$8$};
\node at (4.3,1.8) {$13$};
\node at (5.5,0.4) {$7$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A club has $52$ members. $P$ is the photography group and $A$ is the astronomy group.
Find the number of members in:
a. $P'\cap A$
b. $P\cup A$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,3.8);
\draw (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\node at (1.5,3.3) {$P$};
\node at (4.5,3.3) {$A$};
\node[anchor=north west] at (0.1,3.7) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.7,1.8) {$18$};
\node at (3,1.8) {$9$};
\node at (4.3,1.8) {$?$};
\node at (5.5,0.4) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
a. $P'\cap A$ is the missing region. Subtract the other three regions from the total.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}52-18-9-6\\&=19\end{aligned}$

b. Add the three regions inside the circles.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}18+9+19\\&=46\end{aligned}$

The completed diagram is:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (6,3.8);
\draw (2.2,1.8) circle (1.3);
\draw (3.8,1.8) circle (1.3);
\node at (1.5,3.3) {$P$};
\node at (4.5,3.3) {$A$};
\node[anchor=north west] at (0.1,3.7) {$\xi$};
\node at (1.7,1.8) {$18$};
\node at (3,1.8) {$9$};
\node at (4.3,1.8) {$19$};
\node at (5.5,0.4) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

